  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.94,
      "text": "Welcome back to the show, today we are talking about side projects.",
      "first_word": 0,
      "last_word": 11
    },
    {
      "start": 5.59,
      "end": 11.79,
      "text": "Most people quit in the first three weeks, and it is almost never about talent.",
      "first_word": 12,
      "last_word": 26
    },
    {
      "start": 12.44,
      "end": 18.64,
      "text": "The real reason is that they pick a project whose feedback loop is too slow.",
      "first_word": 27,
      "last_word": 41
    },
    {
      "start": 19.29,
      "end": 25.49,
      "text": "If you cannot see progress in a single evening, your motivation is running on credit.",
      "first_word": 42,
      "last_word": 56
    },
    {
      "start": 26.14,
      "end": 32.34,
      "text": "So the fix is embarrassingly simple, you shrink the loop until it fits one sitting.",
      "first_word": 57,
      "last_word": 71
    },
    {
      "start": 32.99,
      "end": 39.61,
      "text": "I tell people to ship something ugly on day one, then improve it every day after.",
      "first_word": 72,
      "last_word": 87
    },
    {
      "start": 40.26,
      "end": 46.04,
      "text": "The second killer is starting with the hardest part because it feels most impressive.",
      "first_word": 88,
      "last_word": 101
    },
    {
      "start": 46.69,
      "end": 53.31,
      "text": "You should start with the boring part that proves the whole thing can work at all.",
      "first_word": 102,
      "last_word": 117
    },
    {
      "start": 53.96,
      "end": 58.9,
      "text": "There is a myth that discipline is what separates finishers from starters.",
      "first_word": 118,
      "last_word": 129
    },
    {
      "start": 59.55,
      "end": 65.33,
      "text": "In practice it is scope, finishers simply choose smaller things and then expand them.",
      "first_word": 130,
      "last_word": 143
    },
    {
      "start": 65.98,
      "end": 73.02,
      "text": "My rule now is that version one has to run end to end in under a week.",
      "first_word": 144,
      "last_word": 160
    },
    {
      "start": 73.67,
      "end": 79.03,
      "text": "Everything else, all the polish and the features, comes after it already works.",
      "first_word": 161,
      "last_word": 173
    },
    {
      "start": 79.68,
      "end": 85.46,
      "text": "The last trap is telling everyone about the idea before you have built anything.",
      "first_word": 174,
      "last_word": 187
    },
    {
      "start": 86.11,
      "end": 91.89,
      "text": "You get the social reward immediately, and your brain treats the project as done.",
      "first_word": 188,
      "last_word": 201
    },
    {
      "start": 92.54,
      "end": 98.74,
      "text": "So build first, talk later, and let the working thing do the talking for you.",
      "first_word": 202,
      "last_word": 216
    }
  ],
  "duration": 101.39
}